KG42.register("rules-5cb460a0a349744cf78403b5",{"id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R005","paper":"33-retail_market_interoperability","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R005","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Energy-trade execution","process_stage":"activation","market_meaning":"The local MCP informs the H-MG's sale of excess power to other H-MGs or retailers. Scope: H-MG sales of excess generation to other H-MGs or retailers in the proposed local retail market. Condition: The H-MG has excess generation after satisfying its local demand. Retailers purchase the remaining H-MG excess power at the local MCP. Scope: Retailer purchases of H-MG excess power remaining unsold to other H-MGs. Condition: The H-MG's excess power has not been sold to other H-MGs. A H-MG with a power shortage may purchase the cheapest available energy from other H-MGs or retailers. Scope: H-MG purchases from other H-MGs or retailers in the proposed retail market. Condition: The H-MG has a power shortage. This exchange capability requires an energy management system for decision-making in day-ahead and real-time operation. Scope: Energy exchange among adjacent H-MGs connected to the same network through a market operator or similar platform. Condition: A microgrid seeks to sell excess energy to adjacent H-MGs or cover its power shortage through neighbours.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function execution.energy_trade under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["execution.energy_trade","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R005-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"execution.energy_trade","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Energy exchange among adjacent H-MGs connected to the same network through a market operator or similar platform. | H-MG purchases from other H-MGs or retailers in the proposed retail market. | H-MG sales of excess generation to other H-MGs or retailers in the proposed local retail market. | Retailer purchases of H-MG excess power remaining unsold to other H-MGs.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local MCP informs the H-MG's sale of excess power to other H-MGs or retailers. Scope: H-MG sales of excess generation to other H-MGs or retailers in the proposed local retail market. Condition: The H-MG has excess generation after satisfying its local demand.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Retailers purchase the remaining H-MG excess power at the local MCP. Scope: Retailer purchases of H-MG excess power remaining unsold to other H-MGs. Condition: The H-MG's excess power has not been sold to other H-MGs.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"A H-MG with a power shortage may purchase the cheapest available energy from other H-MGs or retailers. Scope: H-MG purchases from other H-MGs or retailers in the proposed retail market. Condition: The H-MG has a power shortage.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"This exchange capability requires an energy management system for decision-making in day-ahead and real-time operation. Scope: Energy exchange among adjacent H-MGs connected to the same network through a market operator or similar platform. Condition: A microgrid seeks to sell excess energy to adjacent H-MGs or cover its power shortage through neighbours.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E03","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p03-c2r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2. H-MG concept","anchor_text":"i.e., generators try to maximize their proﬁt while consumers look hin after minimizing their operati","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In a similar manner to microgrid interoperability, several H-MGs, connected to the same network through a market operator or similar platform, can sell their excess energy to adjacent H-MGs or supply their power shortage through neighbours instead of purchasing energy from retailers. For a microgrid to be able to do this, it is necessary to have an energy management system (EMS) to make decisions in day-ahead and real-time operation. In this paper, every H-MG is assumed to have a home energy management system (HEMS) which is able to send/receive signals to/from a market operator, as explained later in detail. HEMS could functionally be able to predict local load demand, renewable generation, and demand flexibility, and to generate scenarios for the stochastic parameters. The HEMS is physically connected to generation, storage, and DR resources in the H-MG to operate them accordingly, and to the market operator to participate in energy trading. Therefore, HEMS is an integral part of the H-MG concept and the proposed market mechanism in this paper."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3. The proposed retail market structure","anchor_text":"nication channel between H MG and MO, and to operate internal devices upon receiving schedules from ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Interoperability of the H-MGs is yet another feature of the proposed market. When a H-MG comes across excess generation, after satisfying its local demand, it tends to sell excess power to other H-MGs or retailers in the market based on the MCP. Alternatively, a H-MG with power shortage can purchase the cheapest available energy from other H-MGs or retailers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3. The proposed retail market structure","anchor_text":"nication channel between H MG and MO, and to operate internal devices upon receiving schedules from ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"To encourage H-MGs to participate in the market with more local generation, their excess power, which has not been sold to other H-MGs, will be purchased by retailers at the MCP [48]."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No decision variable is defined in the R005 evidence passages. The passages refer qualitatively to excess power, power shortage, cheapest available energy, and sale/purchase execution, but do not assign symbols, domains, units, or optimization roles to those quantities. Declaring an x would require inventing a symbol or domain not present in the frozen graph evidence.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed parameter or constant is defined for R005 in the supplied evidence. MCP is mentioned as a market price at which trades are informed or settled, but it is not defined as a fixed parameter in these passages and has no algebraic value or domain here. Declaring theta would require inventing a parameter meaning, value, or unit."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E11","quote":"When a H-MG comes across excess generation, after satisfying its local demand, it tends to sell excess power to other H-MGs or retailers in the market based on the MCP."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","quote":"To encourage H-MGs to participate in the market with more local generation, their excess power, which has not been sold to other H-MGs, will be purchased by retailers at the MCP [48]."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E11","quote":"Alternatively, a H-MG with power shortage can purchase the cheapest available energy from other H-MGs or retailers."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E03","quote":"several H-MGs, connected to the same network through a market operator or similar platform, can sell their excess energy to adjacent H-MGs or supply their power shortage through neighbours instead of purchasing energy from retailers. For a microgrid to be able to do this, it is necessary to have an energy management system (EMS) to make decisions in day-ahead and real-time operation."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"9b3e81de03465b6753654762304bda57f3118b1125f23608808fe2957afa7d40","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The supplied R005 evidence passages describe qualitative activation behavior: H-MGs with excess generation tend to sell to other H-MGs or retailers at the MCP; retailers purchase unsold excess at the MCP; H-MGs with shortage may purchase the cheapest available energy; and an EMS/HEMS is required for day-ahead and real-time decisions. These passages do not provide an equation, inequality, objective, variable domain, parameter value, or indexed formal relation specific to execution.energy_trade. The existing phi entries are therefore procedural and remain not_formalized with expression null. This is not a claim that the paper lacks mathematics elsewhere; it is only that the frozen R005 node-edge graph and its evidence do not support a formal expression for this activation rule. B evidence remains unreviewed in this experiment, and no independent source audit is claimed.","bindings":[],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
